**Q1.** I would reverse none of the eleven dispositions. The proposed repairs need the qualifications below, especially concerning existing aggregate observations.

For my adopted findings, F1’s replacement comment correctly distinguishes reads from writes: START runs unconditionally at [src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:1860](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:1860). F2 needs only the header correction for the stated mutation family: the sweep does not repaint between transfers, so an escaping fill remains detectable by its final read ([regress/sgi_mte_decline_probe.py:311](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sgi_mte_decline_probe.py:311)). F4’s disclosure accurately limits an oracle that matches phrases rather than numeric values.

I also checked F6 against the scoped working-tree diff: four hunks, 65 additions and 12 deletions, net **+53**. Its rejection stands.

**Q2.**

**(a)** The latch cross is owed. Section 3e explicitly requires the repair path’s CLEAR and SET states. Both returns bypass the destination switch, whose observable labels are A, B, C, LIN_A and LIN_B; its default only prints ([src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:1521](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:1521), [src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:1732](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:1732)).

Thus **2 sites × 5 labels × 2 own-latch states = 20 cells** is complete for this refusal-path enumeration. S2 requires STIPPLE clear; S1 otherwise returns first. The clause does not additionally cross every COPY/depth/mask test inside the skipped arms.

All 20 conditioned variants require individual measurements. Plain exemptions can be recorded as consequences of the concrete paint witnesses, not as additional measured results.

**(b)** Pairing is sound for these single-site variants. S1 sets bit 13; S2 tests bit 14, so S1’s refusal leaves S2’s own latch CLEAR ([src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:182](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:182)). Each transfer needs correct mapping and fresh paint. Linear witnesses must leave COPY clear, depth 8 and the mask full so later declines cannot conceal an escape.

**(c)** **Yes—an existing aggregate observable can change.** `src once` counts the entire transcript and uses final-session `alive` ([regress/sgi_mte_decline_probe.py:271](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sgi_mte_decline_probe.py:271)). Appending three refusals changes a missing-suppression mutant’s count from **7 to 10**. A death in the appended tail can change this row to `"died"`.

